# Java Formatting

When creating or modifying Java source:

- Treat the repository-root `eclipse-codestyle.xml` as the authoritative formatter configuration.
- Use its `P3C-CodeStyle` profile; do not substitute IDE defaults or approximate the style manually.
- Format every Java file changed by the current task before running the final build and tests.
- Limit formatting to Java files touched by the current task; do not mass-reformat unrelated code.
- Preserve behavior while formatting and review the resulting diff for accidental semantic changes.
- If the available formatter cannot load this profile, report the limitation instead of silently using another style.

The profile uses four-space indentation, spaces instead of tabs, and a 120-column line width.
